From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <samucarre@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:47:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] util/Cajon: tooltips and menus open as the bar's
 elastic drawer; menus are the bar's own popover of buttons

util::Cajon<Base> draws a popover scaled vertically from its top edge (which
stays stuck to the bar) while it opens: scaleY 0.12 -> 1.05 -> 1 over 700 ms with
cubic-bezier(.33,.9,.35,1) on each leg, the same "suave" bounce the bar's panels
use (perfilado.py). Only the drawing changes, the popup surface keeps its size.
The tooltip popover (util::Globo) and the module menu use it.

gtkmm only hooks snapshot_vfunc on a derived GType, which it registers when the
object is built through Glib::ConstructParams with a custom type name. Gtk::Popover
is; Gtk::PopoverMenu is not (it wraps a C-created GtkPopoverMenu), so the menu is
now a plain Gtk::Popover with a column of flat buttons (CSS class "elemento") and
separators built from the menu-file entries. A GtkMenuItem with sensitive=False
is an insensitive heading. No action group is needed any more.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
